{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ya9jXpuq72rW35jN4CkCxy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 86,\n3\t \"title\": \"Ticketmaster - blocks electron browserfrom entering presale code\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\nlatest\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nWindows 11 latest\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\nn/a\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nhaving an issue with ticketmaster on electron \\n\\nif you go to this page - https://www.ticketmaster.com/dylan-scott-philadelphia-pennsylvania-02-04-2027/event/0200652AE3A47089\\n\\nand click unlock and enter any presale code, you get a message stating browsing activity paused, i dont get this at all on other browsers, it seems to be detecting something different with electron\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nit should say invalid/valid presale code\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nA minimal sandboxed BrowserWindow using a fresh in-memory session, no preload, no proxy, no request interception and no automation receives HTTP 403 {\\\"response\\\":\\\"block\\\"} from Ticketmaster’s offer-code validation endpoint. The same account, network, event and code work in Chrome and Edge. Tested with Electron 44.4.1 / Chromium 152.0.7977.78.\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n